<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30033" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Murena</span></b>  (old form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Muraena</span></b> ), ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύραινα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The murena</i>, a fish of which the ancients were
			very fond, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 55, 81, § 171</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">muraenam exdorsua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Aul. 2, 9, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Pers. 1, 3, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 5,
			99</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a black stripe in
				the shape of this fish, a black vein in the table-tops of
				citron-wood</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 13, 15, 30, §
		98</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
